  "adaptations": [
    "Reuse the complete Pulse attempt/retry lifecycle with cancellation, concurrent preparation, verification tickets and installation identity fencing.",
    "Retain modern foundation registration custody and exact dead-key/same-key bearer recovery; sequence actual shared credential mutations.",
    "Preserve strict bounded HTTP, canonical bytes, exact response binding, actual server facts and private holder capability lineage.",
    "Keep old Gateway source-compatible DTO facades and actual Pulse custody/holder linkage; no new Vouch or face writes.",
    "Classify the exact sod_encoding_invalid refusal without exporting unknown server prose or changing verification behavior.",
    "Replace scheduler-yield assumptions in the two registration coalescing tests with a private actor-isolated rendezvous: the HTTP release task inherits the registration actor and runs only after the same-actor second caller joins the paused mutation. Production registration behavior, public API and exact key/wire assertions remain unchanged."
  ],
  "qualification": "Provenance records source origins; current-source native receipts and physical acceptance are separate."
}
